{{also|hrat|hrať|hřát}}
==Czech==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|cs|sla-pro|*jьgrati}}. Cognates include Russian {{m|ru|игра́ть}}, Serbo-Croatian {{m|sh|ȉgrati}} and Polish {{m|pl|grać}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Cs-hrát.ogg|audio|lang=cs}}

===Verb===
{{cs-verb|a=i}}

# {{lb|cs|transitive}} to [[play]] {{gloss|a game}}
#: ''Pojďme '''hrát''' Monopoly.'' — ''Let's go and play Monopoly.''
#: '''''Hrajeme''' na schovávanou.'' — ''We're playing hide and seek.''
# {{lb|cs|transitive}} to [[play]] {{gloss|a role}}
# {{lb|cs|transitive}} to [[play]] {{gloss|a musical instrument}}
#: '''''Hraji''' na kytaru.'' — ''I play the guitar.''

